name: Unapproved Scan keeps its refusal readable and preserves existing observations
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/prepared_scan_refusal.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: run agentic-sast:scan {"maxFindings":1}
require-live-snap: 25 PREREQUISITE PLAN | cached-context
expect: recommended reuse
keys: r
require-live-snap: 25 RECORDED ENGINE OUTCOMES | blocked-scan
expect: RESULT blocked
expect: Agentic SAST hunt
expect-not: correlated result status contradicts
expect: details · replay
expect: Esc result actions
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/prepared_scan_refusal.py @TMP_TARGET @ART blocked
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 25 RESULT blocked | result-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 25 RESULT blocked | result-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 25 RESULT blocked | result-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 25 RESULT blocked | result-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 25 RESULT blocked | result-40x12
ask: Does the blocked Scan show a readable outcome at each size and make its allowance guidance reachable without suggesting a completed scan?
nav-mode:
keys: o
require-live-snap: 25 ── REPLAY | compact-result-open
expect: Outcome · blocked
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 25 no model request started | compact-refusal-guidance
resize: 120x36
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 25 preparing model work | preparation-receipt
expect-not: calling model
expect: no model request started
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 Owned first observation | observations-preserved
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/prepared_scan_refusal.py @TMP_TARGET @ART returned
ask: Can the operator distinguish preparation from a request, read the full refusal and return to existing observations without a new decision or automatic work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 15
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
nav-mode:
keys: o
require-live-snap: 25 ── REPLAY | recovered-refusal
expect: Outcome · blocked
expect-not: correlated result status contradicts
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/prepared_scan_refusal.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart recover the same refused job with zero requests, unchanged source and all three original observations?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 15
